---
source: crates/view/tests/today.rs
expression: "portable(&r.html, m.path())"
---
<div class="mv-screen">
<div class="mv-today" data-block="s" data-type="today">
<div class="mv-today-main">
<header class="mv-headline">
<p class="mv-composed bv-meta">Composed by Maestro · <span class="bv-code">the working tree</span> · read now</p>
<h1 class="mv-headline-text">3 things need you. One piece of work is running. One loop has no tick receipts.</h1>
<div class="mv-pills">
<span class="mv-pill" data-tone="attention" data-pill="needs you">
<span class="mv-pill-value">3</span> needs you</span>
<span class="mv-pill" data-tone="success" data-pill="running">
<span class="mv-pill-value">1</span> running</span>
<span class="mv-pill" data-tone="info" data-pill="open asks">
<span class="mv-pill-value">3</span> open asks</span>
<span class="mv-pill" data-tone="danger" data-pill="silent loops">
<span class="mv-pill-value">1</span> silent loops</span>
<span class="mv-pill" data-tone="neutral" data-pill="landing">
<span class="mv-pill-value mv-unavailable">unavailable</span> landing</span>
</div>
</header>
<section class="mv-card bv-card" data-block="today-decision" data-type="top-decision" data-state="partial">
<header class="mv-head">
<h2 class="mv-title">Top decision</h2>
</header>
<div class="mv-top" data-ask="demo-arc.yaml#merge-now">
<p class="mv-row-meta bv-meta">
<span class="mv-badge" data-tone="warning">decision</span> demo · <span class="bv-code">demo-arc.yaml</span> · <span data-tone="attention">blocking</span>
</p>
<p class="mv-ask-title">Merge the demo PR now, or hold for review?</p>
<p class="mv-row-meta bv-meta">asked 22 d ago by demo-arc</p>
<p class="mv-note bv-meta">Answer it in Paseo's Maestro plugin. Maestro answers nothing in this phase.</p>
</div>
<details class="mv-errors">
<summary data-tone="warning">Partial: 2 sources could not be read</summary>
<ul>
<li>
<span class="bv-code">.control/asks/broken.yaml</span>: outside the YAML subset Maestro reads exactly: what this reader's YAML parser refuses (while parsing a flow sequence, expected ',' or ']' at byte 12 line 2 column 1)</li>
<li>
<span class="bv-code">.control/asks/alt-key.yaml#2</span>: entry is not a mapping</li>
</ul>
</details>
<p class="mv-source bv-meta">
<span class="bv-code">worktree:.control/asks</span>
</p>
</section>
<section class="mv-card bv-card" data-block="today-running" data-type="running" data-state="ok">
<header class="mv-head">
<h2 class="mv-title">Running now</h2>
<span class="mv-count">1</span>
</header>
<ul class="mv-list">
<li class="mv-row" data-work="today-run">
<span class="mv-row-title">Round-3 fixes</span>
<span class="mv-row-meta bv-meta">
<span class="mv-chip bv-code">frontier · opus · high</span> claude · mac-studio · budget 48%</span>
</li>
</ul>
<p class="mv-source bv-meta">
<span class="bv-code">fs:<fixture>/work</span>
</p>
</section>
<section class="mv-card bv-card" data-block="today-nodes" data-type="nodes" data-state="unavailable">
<header class="mv-head">
<h2 class="mv-title">Nodes</h2>
<span class="mv-count mv-unavailable">unavailable</span>
</header>
<p class="mv-note" data-tone="danger">Could not be read. This is not the same as none.</p>
<details class="mv-errors">
<summary data-tone="warning">1 source could not be read</summary>
<ul>
<li>
<span class="bv-code">nodes</span>: Maestro reads no node census yet; host adapters bring one (BRO-3276)</li>
</ul>
</details>
<p class="mv-source bv-meta">
<span class="bv-code">nodes</span>
</p>
</section>
</div>
<aside class="mv-rail">
<section class="mv-card bv-card" data-block="health-plan" data-type="plan" data-state="ok">
